From feeb7ef324497c16196037a224baa17a34745a3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:54:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Capture native verification row totals for heterogeneous
 request counts

Copy verification raises a request's maximum width from six to seventeen
rows. Retain the ordinary six-row full-depth row totals (18, 30, 36, 42 on
TP3) with room for any valid request count (min(rows, max_num_reqs), rows),
and use the same shape set for target capture, context capture, and weight
warmup. Compared to request-pinned (num_reqs, 6 * num_reqs) captures,
native-row-only uses fewer FULL graphs (69 vs 70 on TP3, +4 over C40's 65;
84 vs 87 on TP4, +10 over C40's 74), adds zero piecewise graphs, and
removes more row padding when shallower requests sum to a native multiple
of six (e.g. seven requests totaling 36 rows dispatch at 36 instead of 40).

Base: candidate-40 patch head 5f926df6d3126266a9c88c82c06544060008c33c,
tree ca1496c6481dc5bc4b4234b743e4ca023a6c7597, on upstream
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.
Quality: changes capture selection only, with unchanged live arithmetic,
verification policy, and maximum capture rows.
Tests: 70 CPU graph, warmup, and context checks pass; 2-boot GPU qualification
on dgx4 verifies capture time, memory pool delta, and decode latency across
all verification row counts (6, 12, 18, 24, 30, 36, 42, 48).
Upstream status: prepared for review against the pinned candidate source;
not submitted to the canonical upstream and not promoted.

